* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-loop-bandwidth-pm (issue #27, Part of #16)
* Same linearised open-loop AC sweep as tb_loop_ac_real.sp.tmpl, but with the
* loop filter represented by IDEAL R/C elements whose values are supplied by
* the caller (@R1@/@C1@/@C2@) instead of by the real `rppd`/`cap_cmomi`
* compact models.
*
* Why this variant exists (two uses, both stated in ../records/RECORD-001):
*
*   1. MOM-model-uncertainty band. `cap_cmomi` has no corner or mismatch
*      spread in the installed PDK (DR-003 Finding 2), so the +/-20%
*      MOM-uncertainty band the predecessor record
*      (../../sg13cmos5l-loop-filter-momcap/) sweeps cannot be expressed by
*      re-simulating the compact model -- there is no knob on it. Feeding
*      that record's OWN measured C1/C2 values (results.csv, mom_frac
*      -0.20/0.00/+0.20) into an ideal element is the only way to propagate
*      the band into a loop-level f_c / phase-margin number. The nominal
*      (mom_frac = 0) point is cross-checked against the real-subckt
*      testbench, exactly as that record cross-checked its own closed-form
*      fz/fp against a real composite AC sweep.
*
*   2. Filter-resizing proposal. Sweeping R1 above its as-drawn value
*      quantifies how much larger R1*C1 must be for the loop to meet both
*      f_c < f_ref/10 and PM >= 45 deg. Those points are a PROPOSAL, not a
*      measurement of the committed design, and ../corners/proposal.csv keeps
*      them in a separate file for exactly that reason.
*
* Substituted by ../testbench/run.sh: @TEMP@, @R1@, @C1@, @C2@, @KD@, @KV@,
* @INVN@ -- see tb_loop_ac_real.sp.tmpl's header for what each gain means and
* which real measurement each numeric value comes from.

.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@

Vpe pe 0 dc 0 ac 1
Gcp 0 vctrl pe 0 @KD@

* Ideal 2nd-order passive filter: C2 shunt at VCTRL, R1 in series with C1.
R1 vctrl nz @R1@
C1 nz 0 @C1@
C2 vctrl 0 @C2@

Gvco 0 vph vctrl 0 @KV@
Cint vph 0 1
Rleak vph 0 1e15

Ediv fb 0 vph 0 @INVN@

.control
ac dec 200 10 1e9
let mag_ol = mag(v(fb))
let ph_ol = 180*cph(v(fb))/pi
wrdata ac.dat mag_ol ph_ol
.endc
.end
